  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nTrying to use the purge api found here, command claims i have no token even though i do: https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/docs/admin_api/purge_remote_media.rst\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1) Ensure /synapse is mapped.\r\n2) Open a terminal.\r\n3) Drop in this command with your api token:\r\n\r\n$ curl -X POST 'https://matrix.perthchat.org/_synapse/admin/v1/purge_media_cache?before_ts=<1599659116000>?access_token=MDAdefinitely_the_access_token_reeeeeeee'\r\n{\r\n    \"errcode\": \"M_MISSING_TOKEN\",\r\n    \"error\": \"Missing access token\"\r\n}\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: \r\n\r\nperthchat.org\r\n\r\n- **Version**:\r\n\r\nSynapse version 1.19.1\r\n\r\n- **Install method**:\r\n\r\nSpantaleev deploy script.\r\n\r\n- **Platform**:\r\n\r\nDebian 10\r\n",
